From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Raul Hernandez <me@spaceface.dev>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 17:55:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] native_simulator: add a coroutine NCT

nct.c gives each embedded thread a host thread and lets one of them run
at a time. Each embedded context switch then wakes one host thread with
a semaphore and blocks another, through the host's scheduler.

Add nct_coro.c, which implements nct_if.h with stackful coroutines in
the host thread of the embedded CPU. A context switch is a
swapcontext(). errno and the C++ exception state, which are data of the
host thread, are kept for each embedded thread.

It does not depend on how NCE is implemented, and its state is per
instance.

Select it with NSI_NCT=coroutines, in Zephyr with
CONFIG_NATIVE_SIMULATOR_NCT_COROUTINES. Host threads remain the
default. The option's help lists what is lost: host tools see one host
thread, and the embedded threads share its thread-local storage.
---
